cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Absorption Cross-Section Atlas, please cite it as below, for
  the arithmetic only (interpolation, laser-line averages, unit conversion,
  Beer-Lambert absorption, photolysis per pulse). The cross sections are the
  work of the authors of each measurement: cite the original paper named with
  each dataset, and the compilation it came through (listed here).
title: Absorption Cross-Section Atlas
abstract: >-
  A browser tool for gas-phase UV, visible and VUV absorption cross sections of
  about 1000 molecules, from the MPI-Mainz UV/VIS Spectral Atlas (2013
  snapshot), NCAR TUV-x, the Leiden photodissociation and photoionization
  database, IUP Bremen and the Harvard-Smithsonian CfA: datasets overlaid on
  wavelength, wavenumber or photon-energy axes in eleven units, values at laser
  lines with line-width averaging and temperature interpolation, Beer-Lambert
  absorption and the fraction photolyzed by a laser pulse. The data are served
  by cdfoley.com and are not part of the repository.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Foley
    given-names: Casey D.
    website: "https://cdfoley.com"
version: "1.0.3"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/foley-photon/cross-section-atlas"
url: "https://cdfoley.com/beta/cross-sections/"
keywords:
  - absorption cross section
  - UV-visible spectroscopy
  - vacuum ultraviolet
  - photolysis
  - Beer-Lambert law
  - laser photochemistry
  - atmospheric chemistry
